estion/math-academy-id "q-74106" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=4$ and $‖3u+2v‖=17.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $3u$ is orthogonal to $2v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =‖3u{‖}^{2}+‖2v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =(3‖u‖)^{2}+(2‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖3u+2v{‖}^{2} & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (17)^{2} & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4(4)^{2} \\\\ 289 & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+4\\cdot 16 \\\\ 289 & =9‖u{‖}^{2}+64 \\\\ 225 & =9‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74106/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74106"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" :answer/id #uuid "b15d5cb9-0771-5882-9b52-9799560c4883" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264/selection/909eed2d5d2cab4d7b9023f07e338976c62cef4b656570656ea717dda197b241" :answer/id #uuid "a332669e-4c33-5a9a-b676-e08755f41618" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{30}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264/selection/faac4b5dab60d2bcda8e045680b3b3af508bb486fc6da6b2897d26c3338702e9" :answer/id #uuid "4c852026-e34a-5359-a25c-c27a20ddb5bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{41}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "da4cff1c-633c-5daa-b2c6-a12b1dfe29fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264/selection/f50f4f867238a777b4399e5a50d26ffe36b7442e3ee6d4a992e90c76046fab71" :answer/id #uuid "3b5cf131-5b5c-59dc-8868-3fbb8073e006" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{1\\,013}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae948f1d-79d0-56c9-b205-f6111f5db881" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40264/selection/909eed2d5d2cab4d7b9023f07e338976c62cef4b656570656ea717dda197b241" :answer-field/choices ["q-40264/selection/a38ef12f135c1e6010d68ed21f81bc27372a73a756455b7066f6182c46018cc8" "q-40264/selection/909eed2d5d2cab4d7b9023f07e338976c62cef4b656570656ea717dda197b241" "q-40264/selection/faac4b5dab60d2bcda8e045680b3b3af508bb486fc6da6b2897d26c3338702e9" "q-40264/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-40264/selection/f50f4f867238a777b4399e5a50d26ffe36b7442e3ee6d4a992e90c76046fab71"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40264" :question/id #uuid "2fd4f0c8-283c-51b8-8f02-c3a374eace40" :question/math-academy-id "q-40264" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=15$ and $‖u+\\sqrt{5}v‖=75.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{5}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+(\\sqrt{5}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖u+\\sqrt{5}v{‖}^{2} & =‖u{‖}^{2}+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (75)^{2} & =(15)^{2}+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,625 & =225+5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 5\\,400 & =5‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =1\\,080\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=6\\sqrt{30}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40264/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04