:db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-74109" :question/id #uuid "c9c77086-5264-54dd-9623-65feabc3a826" :question/math-academy-id "q-74109" :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖u‖=4$ and $‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v‖=\\sqrt{182}.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $\\sqrt{2}u$ is orthogonal to $\\sqrt{3}v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =‖\\sqrt{2}u{‖}^{2}+‖\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =(\\sqrt{2}‖u‖)^{2}+(\\sqrt{3}‖v‖)^{2} \\\\ ‖\\sqrt{2}u+\\sqrt{3}v{‖}^{2} & =2‖u{‖}^{2}+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (\\sqrt{182})^{2} & =2(4)^{2}+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 182 & =2\\cdot 16+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 182 & =32+3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ 150 & =3‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖v{‖}^{2} & =50\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖v‖=5\\sqrt{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-74109/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-74109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40263/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "a5bc08a9-b6e4-54bc-b4aa-017bd50a47f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40263/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "ef791f48-0f71-5920-95e1-d516d1c7c224" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40263/selection/73eeaf3fae024b54005d89a5185040ad67cf4b6c72d401d6ad32bf0e79c13de9" :answer/id #uuid "72e53761-85c7-5709-8eac-8b72e55471e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40263/selection/9f6bf