" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-40263/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aa4b13a-c222-5a32-b289-04b8c8285d89"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40263"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-39412"] :question/problem "Let $u$ and $v$ be vectors such that $‖v‖=7$ and $‖2u+v‖=25.$  If $u$ is orthogonal to $v$, find $‖u‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ is orthogonal to $v,$ we also have that $2u$ is orthogonal to $v.$ So, the Pythagorean theorem states that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =‖2u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying and substituting in the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =(2‖u‖)^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖2u+v{‖}^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+‖v{‖}^{2} \\\\ (25)^{2} & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+(7)^{2} \\\\ 625 & =4‖u{‖}^{2}+49 \\\\ 576 & =4‖u{‖}^{2} \\\\ ‖u{‖}^{2} & =144\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $‖u‖=12.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-74177/selection/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "bb50243f-f27a-5732-ad22-fdb761c767b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74177/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "1cc2ad41-9941-5d2c-99dd-ecf427cd2971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74177/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "d22db3fc-4ed3-5008-9174-cb97b678adff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-74177/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "166b41b6-702c-5823-9970-5e6c4876a760" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7